From 134bb6efe45783f4abd8d655eedecf90c24bc249 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:45:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] build: include <string.h> for strcmp in _core.c

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted; this port's automation may not open issues or PRs on repos other than riseproject-dev/python-wheels]

_core.c's healpix_cone_search() calls strcmp() without declaring it,
relying on another header to pull in <string.h> transitively. GCC has
long warned on implicit function declarations, but GCC 14
(quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_39_riscv64, Rocky Linux 10's system GCC) turns
that warning into a hard error, so the build fails there even though it
succeeds on the older GCC upstream's own manylinux2014 image ships:

    astropy_healpix/_core.c:366:13: error: call to undeclared library
    function 'strcmp' with type 'int (const char *, const char *)'

Add the missing include.
---
 astropy_healpix/_core.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/astropy_healpix/_core.c b/astropy_healpix/_core.c
index 30906e4..2e3b7b8 100644
--- a/astropy_healpix/_core.c
+++ b/astropy_healpix/_core.c
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 #include <Python.h>
+#include <string.h>
 #include <math.h>
 #include <numpy/arrayobject.h>
 #include <numpy/ufuncobject.h>
-- 
